At this call site:

```java
List<BlockNode> successors = includeExcHandlers
    ? child.getSuccessors()
    : child.getCleanSuccessors();
```

we care about the `false` branch of the ternary (`child.getCleanSuccessors()`), i.e. the case where `includeExcHandlers` is `false`.

The implementation of `getCleanSuccessors()` is:

```java
public List<BlockNode> getCleanSuccessors() {
    return this.cleanSuccessors;
}
```

So the method will return `null` exactly when the field `cleanSuccessors` is `null`.

From the provided codebase:

- Many call sites explicitly handle the possibility that `getCleanSuccessors()` returns `null`, e.g.:

  ```java
  List<BlockNode> successors = block.getCleanSuccessors();
  if (successors == null || successors.size() >= 2) { ... }
  ```

  and

  ```java
  List<BlockNode> successors = block.getCleanSuccessors();
  if (successors == null) {
      return null;
